WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:07.230
In the seventh Gunpla Building Contest, the Master Cup, the Grand Prix goes to...

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.610
Entry number eight!

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.950
Sakai Minato from Osaka Prefecture!

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.160
Alright!

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.040
Wow! Those hotties look somewhat familiar.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.710
There's my master, too.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.290
Congratulations.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.760
You're truly an ultra super deluxe great special modeler. Minato!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.800
My work doesn't even come close.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.010
You're a good sport, Yuuma.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.100
Who's that you're with?

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.810
What a funny face.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.690
Minato.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.020
Hmm?

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.650
You made such an awesome Gunpla.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.480
How cool of you.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.360
Won't you customize me as well?

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.780
Just kidding!

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.820
I'll do it, I'll do it! I'll tune you up just the way I like it!

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.370
I'll start with your joints here.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:02.870
I'll replace the polycaps and...

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.300
Darn, it was suck a great dream.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.840
Oh yeah, the results of the Tokyo qualifiers should be in!

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.220
I bet Yuuma's team has lost already.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.140
They should be in tears.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.390
Wait, they won!

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.600
Is Yuuma really so eager to avoid the Master Cup!?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.100
Doesn't he want to face me?

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.520
That punk!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.920
The private Gunpla Academy...

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.210
Last year's national champion team.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.090
Don't tell me you were in last year's tournament?

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.340
Well, yeah, sort of.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.180
I-It's true.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.310
I-Is that so...

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.980
Obviously, my Zeo Zeong couldn't help but lose against

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.940
a member of last year's national champion team.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.860
Isn't that right? Right!

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.480
Sudou, do you think...?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.690
Yeah, We can win the West Tokyo qualifiers.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.530
Never mind these trifles, Mr. President.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.120
We're after the national championship, not the regional qualifiers, right?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.200
It's not that simple.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:55.750
Sure it is. With my Gunpla and yours...

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.260
Wow, this is well-made.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.140
From the style, it seems like it's from the Kansai area.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.050
Is this the work of the Shingyo school?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.600
You got that right.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.520
What an interesting school I've transferred to.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.150
My luck must be improving,

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.690
if I get to battle with such a lovely lady.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.690
What are you saying, you idiot!?

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.200
By this weekend, the best 4 in the qualifiers will be decided,

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.330
and the brackets will be drawn.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.920
Who will be our opponent?

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:45.680
We now begin match four of the quarterfinals round of the West Tokyo qualifiers.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.970
<i>Field 5, City.</i>

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.640
We're at the destination point.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.980
The enemy should come from the sea.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.280
I'll get into shooting position.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.400
With this Super Xamel that's been made even larger than legal mobile armor size,

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:10.870
we'll show you our tank spirit!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.170
Wh-What?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.210
This is...

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.090
the mobile armor Doggorla!

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.760
Open fire!

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.320
Where's the Doggorla?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.240
Where'd it go?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.170
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:05.920
The winner of match four is Suiryu Academy's team Leviathan.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.260
What's that Gunpla that looks like a dragon?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.350
It's the Doggorla from V Gundam.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.140
They're a team that controls one mobile armor with three people.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.190
With this, the best four are decided.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.280
Let's go. It's time to draw the brackets.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.230
Yes, sir!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:31.200
The teams advancing to the semifinals of the West Tokyo qualifiers

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.120
in the Gunpla Battle Japanese Championship are...

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.790
Seiho Academy Middle School, team Try Fighters.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.460
St. Odessa Girls' School, team Song Dynasty Vase.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.920
Suiryu Academy, team Leviathan.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:47.550
And Miyazato Institute High School, team G-Master.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.720
What are  Sakashita and Suga doing...?

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:56.390
We will now draw lots decide the brackets for the semifinals.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:10.570
And here are the semifinals brackets.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.950
We're in the first match.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.740
Against Suiryu Academy...

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.790
Those dragon-users?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:23.330
Miss Kaoruko, our opponent is that Miyazato Institute.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:24.920
They're formidable enemies.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.000
Pretty strong.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.340
Sure they are.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.550
Miyazato was last year's regional champion team, after all.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.930
This is the first time we'll face you.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.350
Nice to meet you.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:44.110
Who cares if you're last year's champion team? We're gonna win.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.780
Don't underestimate us because we're younger, and we're girls.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:52.240
I know Gunpla Battle's not that easy.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:56.080
Besides, we're fighting against the little sister of Susumu Sazaki,

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.200
who made it to the best 16 in the 10th world championship.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.920
You know my brother?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.290
I fought him when I was in middle school.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.050
He had a great Gyan and a great shield...

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:12.840
I was wiped out.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:19.060
Then his sister will let you taste the defeat once again.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.890
I'd rather not.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.310
I've been training hard, you know.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:24.980
Well then, until tomorrow.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.070
Wow, they're psyching each other out!

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.900
You're serious, Gyanko.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.320
Is she really that confident she's going to win?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.820
Or is it...

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:41.540
Our opponent is Suiryu Academy. They're tough to beat.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.830
We're aware of that.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:47.420
Get some rest today, and prepare for tomorrow's battle.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:48.420
Yes, sir!

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:52.170
I won't make another blunder like I did in the quartefinals.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.220
Me neither!

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:54.800
That's the spirit.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.640
Huh? Is that...

00:08:58.930 --> 00:08:59.810
Gyanko?

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:04.770
What the--?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.690
Sekai! Sekai!

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:08.360
What is it?

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:11.820
We've been matched up with the Miyazato Institute.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.530
I won't be able to fight you again.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.330
Hold on, you haven't even started fighting yet

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:22.290
But they're last year's champion team!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.370
Why have you turned so wimpy?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.170
Why wouldn't I...

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.500
Sekai, we'll leave Gyanko to you.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.170
What!?

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.210
Let's go.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:34.260
Roger.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.130
Wh-What? Wait. Wait, Hoshino.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:39.640
Yuuma! Mr. Ral!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.470
Fumina, you don't mind?

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.940
I'm trying to help our enemy this once.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:52.110
I know the pressure of fighting against the Miyazato Institute,

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.610
last year's champion school.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.200
Hey, drink this. It's my treat.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:02.490
It's for the lunch you made for the other day.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.960
If you don't want it, I'll...

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.210
So you do want it.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.010
Look, cheer up.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.680
Or you'll lose before the fight.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.260
My master told me,

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:26.890
however tough your opponent, you need a fighting spirit to win.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:27.640
Then...

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.020
Then give me some fighting spirit.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.520
What? How...?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.110
Tomorrow, if my team wins, will you go on a date with me?

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:37.740
What!?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.950
Will you... go on a date with me?

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.200
Miss Kaoruko has gone behind enemy lines.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.040
How exciting.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.000
I have to go on a date again?

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.080
"Again?"

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.670
What do you mean? Are you dating somebody?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.050
Umm...

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:57.840
It's Miss Hoshino, isn't it?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:02.470
Do you have a cold? Please mind your health.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.600
I don't think it's a cold...

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.440
So much for the tender and mopey sympathy-gaining strategy!

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:16.980
I, Sazaki Kaoruko, will win both tomorrow's battle and your heart!

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.700
You... weren't you feeling down?

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:22.360
Huh? Well...

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:28.080
You're flirting with boys on the day before the semifinals.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.710
You must take us lightly.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.120
You're from the Miyazato Institute... ?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:35.210
I'm Sakashita. Sakashita Yomi.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.840
Sorry to keep you waiting, my dear Yomi!

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.800
You're with a guy as well!

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.390
No, I'm making him buy me dinner for being so late.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.890
Oh, come now, Yomi!  you're being shy.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:50.520
Stop acting like there's something between us!

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.490
Team G-Master from the Miyazato Institute...

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:04.460
You came late to the drawing of the semifinals brackets.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:07.410
Last year's winners are that confident?

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.340
No, that's not it.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:13.460
Our transfer student came late, and that just held us up.

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:18.010
Aren't you the one who's taking us lightly?

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:22.370
Even though you're facing us tomorrow, you're going out with boys.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.160
No, no, this isn't a date.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:30.430
I can't believe you're our opponent in the semifinals.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:31.990
What do you mean?

00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:34.030
I'm saying there's no challange.

00:12:34.030 --> 00:12:35.310
What did you say!?

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:35.990
Hey,

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:36.480
Hmm?

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.030
don't look down on her like that.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:42.070
She's serious about Gunpla Battle.

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:46.700
When I fought against her once, my fist heard her feelings.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.020
Wh-What are you saying?

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.260
I mean, don't underestimate her.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.650
Sekai...

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.370
I'm going home to prep for tomorrow.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.880
Gyanko, let's meet in the final match!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.870
I don't care if they're last year's champion team. Don't lose to those guys.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:04.300
Of course not!

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:08.630
I swear on my Gunpla... No, upon my shield!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.220
It's a promise!

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.340
Yeah... I promise!

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:15.890
Hey, kid!

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:19.820
I'm not a kid. My name is Kamiki Sekai.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:22.660
You're a member of team Try Fighters, right?

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:24.070
Yeah.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.710
I saw your battle on video.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.780
You use some interesting techniques.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.910
The Jigen Haoh style of kenpo.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.060
You know it?

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.780
It won't work on me, though.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:41.900
Well, before that, good luck in the semifinals.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.300
Kamiki Sekai.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:47.310
Who... are you?

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.370
Me? I'm Suga.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:53.640
Suga Akira.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:05.630
Hoshino?

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:09.410
What's up?

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:13.080
It... It's nothing, but...

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:16.680
I was wondering what you and Gyanko talked about.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:19.110
Please listen to me, Hoshino.

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.530
She was faking being depressed.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.660
I regret treating her to a cup of juice.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:25.060
Is that right...

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.130
Didn't she know that kind of trick would backfire with you?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:31.950
Hoshino.

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:32.860
What is it?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.730
I promised Gyanko I'd see her in the final match.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.680
So let's be sure to win tomorrow!

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.520
Yeah, let's do our best!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:50.610
<i>We now begin the semifinals     of the West Tokyo qualifiers.</i>

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.300
<i>This is match one.</i>

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.250
Guys, do you hear me?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.780
The Doggorla has separating functions. Keep that in mind!

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:07.530
Right.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:08.300
Roger that.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.500
Sekai, I'm carrying you for a reason.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.590
Do your job.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:13.950
I know that!

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:14.600
It's coming!

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:16.190
I'll open fire.

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:18.880
Sekai!

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:27.870
It separated.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:28.730
Now!

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:53.450
Were they waiting for us to separate?

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.430
President, the red one's gone!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.810
What? Where is it!?

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:57.540
It's above us!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:06.570
Winning Knuckle!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:15.580
Jigen Haoh style! Shippu-Zuki!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:15.580
<i>Shippu-Zuki: Gale Punch</i>

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.070
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.580
The winner is team Try Fighters from Seiho Academy.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:33.860
Miss Kaoruko, Sekai's team won!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:35.450
They're advancing to the final round!

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:36.350
Right.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:37.220
Gyanko!

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:40.510
I'll be waiting for you at the final match.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.850
You got it. I'll keep my promise.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:45.900
I swear upon this shields!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:52.240
<i>And now for match two of the semifinals round of the West Tokyo qualifiers.</i>

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:56.890
<i>Team Song Dynasty Vase from St. Odessa Girls' School.</i>

00:16:56.890 --> 00:17:01.080
<i>versus team G-Master from the Miyazato Institute High School.</i>

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:04.800
<i>Gunpla Battle, combat mode, start up.</i>

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:08.090
<i>Model damage level, set to B.</i>

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.160
<i>Please set your GP Base.</i>

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:15.100
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.450
<i>Field 1, Space.</i>

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:21.680
<i>Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.220
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:36.120
R-Gyagya, Sazaki Kaoruko, plus two others.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:37.160
Miss Kaoruko!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.380
That's too abbreviated.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:39.950
I'll keep my promise!

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:49.660
The Miyazato Institute has changed all its machines.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:52.700
A V Gundam... and a customized G-Fighter.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.160
What's that one based on the Hyaku-Shiki?

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.280
Can you tell, Yuuma?

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:00.540
Yes.

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:03.360
I recognized it straight away.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.390
That Hyaku-Shiki was made by

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.190
Sakai Minato of the Gunpla Shingyo school!

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:12.010
How's the Mega-shiki?

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:13.580
It's highly satisfactory.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.250
So much so that I can't control my emotions!

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:21.120
Attacking from this range!?

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.480
So many particles! Is it a high mega--!?

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:33.860
Mahiru!

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.110
With a single shot!

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:39.460
What performance!

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:41.430
How could you!

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:46.930
Get out of the way!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.420
So you were bluffing after all.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.730
What did you say!?

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:54.690
I thought you were tougher. You were even dating they day before.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.360
That has nothing to do with this!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.190
What was it again, "my fist heard her feelings"?

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:10.210
Hey, hey. I haven't had my turn yet.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:19.370
It isn't shooting!? That G-Fighter is toying with me!

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:25.490
How dare you ignore me!

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:28.880
Oops.

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:40.590
My arm!?

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:45.910
Yes, this is just a game.

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:51.390
This is a Gunpla Battle, you know.

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:58.260
Miss Kaoruko!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.840
Keiko!

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:01.830
Sekai?

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:05.930
That fighter... it used martial arts.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:12.640
Jigen Haoh style of kenpo, right?

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.680
It won't work on me, though.

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.550
Suga Akira.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:22.840
All that's left is that stubborn chick.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.080
Not bad.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:35.240
Ah yes, it's a great shield.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.750
Worthy of Susumu Sazaki's little sister.

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:41.780
But... what if I have a sword that exceeds its defensive strength!?

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.290
There's no paradox!

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.140
My shields!?

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:11.990
Why... My R-Gyagya!

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:21.040
My shields have been...

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:30.870
I'm sorry, Sekai.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.760
I couldn't keep my promise...

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:48.950
Gyanko.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.610
Gyanko!

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:34.970
What a surprise.

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:40.590
The Sleggar who transferred is now playing for a Tokyo school.

00:23:43.260 --> 00:23:46.480
Will his existence be a threat to us?

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.220
No it won't, Uncle.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.240
Don't call me that here.

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:54.910
My apologies.

00:23:56.320 --> 00:23:58.040
Coach Allan Adams.

00:24:00.650 --> 00:24:02.390
It's time for the final match at last.

00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:05.300
I'll get revenge for Gyanko, and go to the national tournament.

00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:07.070
Next Episode, "Showdown At Solomon".

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:09.340
My Jigen Haoh style doesn't work?
